{"id":"NCT07890610","title":"Physiology-directed Epinephrine Dosing in Pediatric Cardiac Arrest","official":"Physiology-directed Epinephrine Dosing in Pediatric Cardiac Arrest","summary":"This is a prospective, observational, multi-center cohort study of pediatric cardiac arrests. The purpose of this study is to evaluate the physiologic response to epinephrine as an outcome discriminator in pediatric in-hospital cardiac arrest (IHCA). In addition, the investigators will determine optimal epinephrine dosing strategies based on the initial physiologic response to epinephrine, and to develop machine learning (ML) algorithms to guide intra-arrest therapy.","conditions":["Cardiac Arrest (CA)"],"interventions":[],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Arrest in an ICU\n* Patients received chest compressions for at least 1 minute\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Lack of commitment to aggressive therapies (e.g., CPR performed as part of end-of-life care)\n* Brain death determination prior to CPR\n* Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest was the reason for initial admission to the hospital (known poor outcomes)\n* Supported by Veno-Arterial Extra Corporeal Membrane Oxygenation at the start of CPR","minAge":"37 Weeks","maxAge":"18 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":1620,"start":"2024-07-01","pcd":"2029-06-30","upd":"2026-10-22","sponsor":"Children's Hospital of Philadelphia","areas":["other"],"central":["Jessica Goldstein · 215-590-1859 · goldsteij1@chop.edu","CHOP RSC Clinical Research Program Manager · 215-590-1859 · grahamk1@chop.edu"],"sites":[{"f":"CHOC","city":"Orange","pr":"California","zip":"92868","s":"R","lat":33.7878,"lon":-117.8531,"c":"Jennifer Hayes · 909-614-3592 · jhayes@choc.org"},{"f":"Stanford Medicine Children's Health","city":"Stanford","pr":"California","zip":"94305","s":"R","lat":37.4241,"lon":-122.1661,"c":"Felice Su · 650-736-7632 · felicesu@stanford.edu"},{"f":"Children's Hospital Colorado","city":"Denver","pr":